@REM Phase 12 — Windows Scheduled Task template.
@REM
@REM This is a reference template for creating a Windows Scheduled Task
@REM via schtasks.exe or Task Scheduler GUI. It runs sync-pending every
@REM 5 minutes.
@REM
@REM Usage:
@REM   1. Replace {{PROJECT_ROOT}} with the absolute path to hermes-agent
@REM      (e.g. D:\hermes-agent)
@REM   2. Replace {{PYTHON}} with the python.exe path
@REM      (e.g. D:\hermes-agent\.venv\Scripts\python.exe)
@REM   3. Replace {{USERNAME}} with the Windows user account
@REM
@REM Create:
@REM   schtasks /create /tn "LocalAPI Sync Trigger" ^
@REM     /tr "{{PYTHON}} -m local_api.scripts.sync_trigger sync-pending --limit 10" ^
@REM     /sc minute /mo 5 ^
@REM     /ru {{USERNAME}} ^
@REM     /f
@REM
@REM Dry-run variant:
@REM   schtasks /create /tn "LocalAPI Sync Trigger (dry-run)" ^
@REM     /tr "{{PYTHON}} -m local_api.scripts.sync_trigger sync-pending --limit 10 --dry-run" ^
@REM     /sc minute /mo 30 ^
@REM     /ru {{USERNAME}} ^
@REM     /f
@REM
@REM Delete:
@REM   schtasks /delete /tn "LocalAPI Sync Trigger" /f
@REM
@REM Query:
@REM   schtasks /query /tn "LocalAPI Sync Trigger"
@REM
@REM Logs are written to: %TEMP%\sync_trigger_schtask.log
@REM (adjust StandardOutPath if using XML import)
@REM
@REM DO NOT execute — reference only.
